    "created_at": "2020-05-28T16:27:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-05-28T16:27:20Z",
    "body": "> I have two stack repos where one has docker enabled. I ran `stack --no-install-ghc --lock-file read-only ghc -- --numeric-version` on both repos.\r\n> \r\n> * No docker: 0.37s\r\n> * With docker: 1.40s\r\n> \r\n> Is this reproducible, and if so is adding `--no-docker` an option?\r\n\r\nWe can definitely add the `--no-docker` argument if that resolves the issue. I don't use Haskell/Stack so my knowledge on this comes from a quick skim of the [stack docker integration docs](https://docs.haskellstack.org/en/stable/docker_integration/) but does this still give the correct version number if someone has enabled docker in the `stack.yaml`?\r\n\r\n> Yeah, this is definitely an issue with ghc itself. I was talking to matchai the other day and he said it could be a good idea to cache the Haskell version on first load; or grab it async.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately those two options are still a little bit off as currently starship is stateless so we have no way to cache data between runs of the prompt or fetch some information in the background. There have been discussions before about how to implement this but for some reason I can't find them at the moment 😞 .",
