    "created_at": "2020-06-10T10:25:55Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-06-10T10:25:55Z",
    "body": "It would seem that Stack is no stranger to [performance issues](﻿﻿https://github.com/commercialhaskell/stack/labels/type%3A%20performance). Some of these have been open for more than a few years---unless the sufficiently smart Haskell compiler is coming out soon, I think caching will likely be the only way around this one.\r\n\r\nFWIW, on my system, `stack --no-install-ghc --lock-file read-only ghc -- --numeric-version` takes about 400ms, while `ghc --numeric-version` takes about 100ms (250ms if the executable's been kicked out of the system cache), so even if we completely got rid of the stack overhead, this would *still* be much slower than I'm comfortable having for a language module.",
